T*
(Livox MID-360 Step-by-Step Guide) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This guide walks through Livox MID-360 bring-up in this repository from a fresh host:) Tj
T*
(network setup, SDK install, configuration, live verification, ROS driver usage, and the) Tj
T*
(local Python viewer and SLAM demos.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This guide is based on the local repo files docs/lidar_cheatsheet.html,) Tj
T*
(docs/lidar_docs.html, scripts/navigation/slam/livox2_python.py,) Tj
T*
(scripts/navigation/slam/livox_python.py, scripts/sensors/live_points.py,) Tj
T*
(scripts/navigation/slam/live_slam.py, and scripts/navigation/slam/mid360_config.json.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Before You Start) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ItemExpected Value) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(LiDAR modelLivox MID-360) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(LiDAR IP192.168.123.120) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Typical host IP192.168.123.222) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recommended SDKLivox-SDK2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Repo root in this workspace/home/melodse/ef_ws/g1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The local Python viewer and SLAM scripts assume the host is on the 192.168.123.0/24 network) Tj
T*
(and that the LiDAR points at that host IP in its JSON config.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 1. Connect the LiDAR Network) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Place the host PC and MID-360 on the same subnet.) Tj
ET
