() Tj
T*
(- Connect Ethernet from the G-1 shoulder port or Livox network path to your PC.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Find your network interface name with ip addr.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Assign the host interface an address like 192.168.123.222/24.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Ping the MID-360 at 192.168.123.120.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ip addr) Tj
T*
(sudo ip addr add 192.168.123.222/24 dev <your_nic>) Tj
T*
(ping 192.168.123.120) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Expected result: the sensor responds to ping and the link stays up.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 2. Install Base Build Tools) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Install the tools needed to build Livox SDKs and inspect traffic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(sudo apt update) Tj
T*
(sudo apt install git build-essential cmake tcpdump) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 3. Build and Install Livox-SDK2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Install the recommended vendor SDK used by the repos main Livox wrapper.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(cd ~) Tj
T*
(git clone https://github.com/Livox-SDK/Livox-SDK2.git) Tj
T*
(cd Livox-SDK2) Tj
T*
(mkdir build) Tj
T*
(cd build) Tj
T*
(cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release) Tj
T*
(make -j$\(nproc\)) Tj
T*
(sudo make install) Tj
T*
(sudo ldconfig) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Expected result: the system can locate liblivox_lidar_sdk.so or) Tj
T*
(liblivox_lidar_sdk_shared.so.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 4. Create a Python Environment) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Install Python dependencies used by the local Livox scripts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(cd /home/melodse/ef_ws/g1) Tj
T*
(python3 -m venv .venv) Tj
T*
(source .venv/bin/activate) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
