(Bring up the official ROS1 driver if you want a /livox/lidar topic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(source /opt/ros/noetic/setup.bash) Tj
T*
(mkdir -p ~/catkin_ws/src) Tj
T*
(cd ~/catkin_ws/src) Tj
T*
(git clone https://github.com/Livox-SDK/livox_ros_driver2.git) Tj
T*
(cd livox_ros_driver2) Tj
T*
(./build.sh ROS1) Tj
T*
(cd ~/catkin_ws) Tj
T*
(catkin_make -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DROS_EDITION=ROS1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Add these lines to ~/.bashrc if you use the driver repeatedly:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(source /opt/ros/noetic/setup.bash) Tj
T*
(source ~/catkin_ws/devel/setup.bash) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 14. Configure the ROS Driver JSON) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Point the ROS driver at the correct LiDAR IP and host IP.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(mkdir -p ~/livox_cfg) Tj
T*
(cp ~/catkin_ws/src/livox_ros_driver2/config/MID360_config.json ~/livox_cfg/) Tj
T*
(nano ~/livox_cfg/MID360_config.json) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Make sure the following values are correct:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- lidar_configs[0].ip = 192.168.123.120) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- host_net_info.*_ip = your host IP) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- pcl_data_type = 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 15. Launch the ROS Driver) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Publish the Livox stream into ROS.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(roslaunch livox_ros_driver2 msg_MID360.launch \\) Tj
T*
(user_config_path:=/home/$USER/livox_cfg/MID360_config.json \\) Tj
T*
(xfer_format:=0 data_src:=0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Expected log lines:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([ INFO] Connect lidar: 192.168.123.120 ...) Tj
T*
([ INFO] Init lidar success) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 16. Verify the ROS Topic) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
ET
endstream
